    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLNote</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>330</x>
      <y>180</y>
      <w>720</w>
      <h>230</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>Two ways to trigger the recovery,
- Automatic recovery: not supported for now
- Operators manually trigger the recovery by adding annotation operator.etcd.io/recover-cluster-from
  into EtcdCluster, the value is the member ordinal from which to recover the cluster.

We can record the following status for users reference, but the controller shouldn't depend
on them to make decision, instead it gets the status from live environment.
- LastRecoveryTime
- RecoveryCount
- LastReveredFrom  

We don't need to add other members into the cluster. Instead, we use the existing scale in/out
process to take care of it.
bg=blue</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
